# Set database access controls
# Variables: LDAP_ADMIN_DN, LDAP_BASE_DN, READ_SUBJECT
#
# IMPORTANT: only attributes that exist in the *already loaded* schema may
# appear in "to attrs=". OpenLDAP resolves those names when the ACL is parsed
# and rejects the whole modify with "unknown attr ... in to clause" otherwise.
#
# This is why "shadowLastChange" was removed from rule {0}: it comes from
# nis.schema, which is not loaded by default - and schemas are loaded *after*
# this step runs, so it could never be valid here even with
# INCLUDE_SCHEMAS=nis. That single unknown attribute made the entire modify
# fail atomically, so no ACL was ever applied and the data database silently
# fell back to OpenLDAP's default access policy. If you load nis.schema and
# want shadowLastChange protected, add it with a second ldapmodify at the end
# of initialisation.
#
# Order matters: the first matching "by" clause wins, so the replicator read
# grant must precede "by * none".
#
# userPassword: the replicator needs "read" (not just "auth") or passwords will
# not replicate and a promoted replica cannot serve binds. The local root
# identity is deliberately NOT granted userPassword read - it does not need it.
#
# The peercred root identity (gidNumber=0+uidNumber=0,cn=peercred,cn=external,
# cn=auth) is granted read on the data tree so that operational tooling run via
# `docker exec` (healthcheck.sh, ldapcheck.sh) can verify suffix and contextCSN
# state without embedding an administrator password in a probe. Anyone able to
# run docker exec as root can already read the LMDB files directly, so this does
# not widen the practical trust boundary. It is the same identity that
# configure-monitor.ldif already uses for cn=Monitor.
#
# READ_SUBJECT defaults to "users" - any authenticated principal may read the
# whole directory. Set LDAP_READ_ACCESS_SUBJECT to a group selector, e.g.
#   group.exact="cn=ldap-readers,ou=Group,<base>"
# to restrict reads to a group.
dn: olcDatabase={2}mdb,cn=config
changetype: modify
add: olcAccess
olcAccess: {0}to attrs=userPassword by dn="{{LDAP_ADMIN_DN}}" write by dn.exact="cn=replicator,{{LDAP_BASE_DN}}" read by anonymous auth by self write by * none
-
add: olcAccess
olcAccess: {1}to dn.base="" by * read
-
add: olcAccess
olcAccess: {2}to * by dn="{{LDAP_ADMIN_DN}}" write by dn.base="gidNumber=0+uidNumber=0,cn=peercred,cn=external,cn=auth" read by dn.exact="cn=replicator,{{LDAP_BASE_DN}}" read by {{READ_SUBJECT}} read by * none
